Below is the exact request you’d send to VirusTotal’s v3 API to fetch **subdomain** relationships for `example.org`, limited to 10 results and starting at the cursor `abc`.  
(Replace `my_api` with your actual API key.)

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/relationships/subdomains?limit=10&continuation_cursor=abc
Host: www.virustotal.com
x-apikey: my_api
Accept: application/json
```

---

### Sample Response (JSON)

> *Note: This is a mock example illustrating the structure of the data you’ll receive. Your real response may differ in content.*

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "sub1.example.org",
      "type": "subdomain",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": {
          "harmless": 12,
          "malicious": 0,
          "suspicious": 1,
          "undetected": 5,
          "timeout": 0
        },
        "last_analysis_date": 1700000000,
        "last_analysis_results": { /* ... */ }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sub2.example.org",
      "type": "subdomain",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": {
          "harmless": 9,
          "malicious": 1,
          "suspicious": 0,
          "undetected": 7,
          "timeout": 0
        },
        "last_analysis_date": 1699999000,
        "last_analysis_results": { /* ... */ }
      }
    }
    /* ... up to 10 items total ... */
  ],
  "links": {
    "self": "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/relationships/subdomains?limit=10&continuation_cursor=abc"
  },
  "meta": {
    "continuation_cursor": "defghijklmnopqrs",
    "total_count": 42
  }
}
```

#### What you’ll get

- **IDs**: Each item’s `"id"` field contains the subdomain name (e.g., `"sub1.example.org"`).
- **Context Attributes**: The `"attributes"` section includes useful metadata such as:
  - `last_analysis_stats`: Counts of harmless/malicious/suspicious/undetected/timeout detections.
  - `last_analysis_date`: Unix timestamp of the last analysis.
  - `last_analysis_results`: Detailed per-engine results (you can ignore this if you only need high‑level stats).

If you only need the IDs and the context attributes, you can extract those fields from each object in the `"data"` array. The `"meta.continuation_cursor"` value (`"defghijklmnopqrs"` in the example) tells you where to start the next page of results.
